        "content": "<p>Consider</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- error: Missing cases: -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nofun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>nofun</code> succeeds, creates a sorry (within a match lemma), and logs an error. <code>first</code> doesn't make it to <code>trivial</code>.</p>\n<p>Even though <code>exact</code> seems to impose <code>withoutErrToSorry</code>, <code>nofun</code> seems to log an error and succeed with a sorry anyway. Perhaps its elaborator ought to respect <code>errToSorry</code> and throw when it's <code>false</code> instead?</p>",
